<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacques Lauriston</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1768">1768</a>–<a href="/years/1828">1828</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Jacques Law de Lauriston</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacques Lauriston was a French general and diplomat of Scottish descent and an aide-de-camp of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. In May 1806 he occupied Ragusa with French troops and withstood a siege by Russian and Montenegrin forces until relieved. He served as ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1811–1812, was captured at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> in 1813 and, under the restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a>, became a marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1823.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacques-lauriston.jpg" alt="Jacques Lauriston" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After François Gérard / Marie-Éléonore Godefroid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacques_Alexandre_Law_de_Lauriston_(Godefroid).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In May 1806 French troops under General <b>Jacques Lauriston</b> occupied Ragusa, ostensibly to protect it from the Russians, and the city was besieged by Russian and Montenegrin forces, which devastated its territory.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-ragusa">Republic of Ragusa · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pondicherry">Pondicherry</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=11.93,79.83&amp;year=1807" aria-label="Pondicherry on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6745 1719 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Jacques Lauriston"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7195 1989h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7195 1989h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=11.93,79.83&amp;year=1807">What was here in 1807? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
